vkquake-ios overlay 0020: R2.1 device-round fixes + R3 holsters.

Four defects the user found on the M5 Vision Pro on 2026-08-10, root-caused
rather than tuned around, plus charter A7's holster system.

FIX 1 - standing eye height. Quake's camera sits 46 units above the floor
(24 hull mins + 22 view_ofs) = 1.17 m at the default world scale, so in VR
you stand in a pit. The rise is now DERIVED: the shell publishes the
tracking alignment's height (the player's real eye height in metres) and
the engine puts the camera exactly that high in game units. the user's
+22.0 in of manual trim falls out of the formula, and so does
QuakeQuest's opposite framing (world scale 26.25, rise ~0). Clamped
against low ceilings by a trace, because the raised camera is 12 units
above the player hull's own head.

FIX 2 - "the gun shoots low", two independent causes:
  (a) V_DriftPitch. cl.nodrift is false out of CL_ClearState, so pitch
      drift runs from the first frame of every map and drags the SENT
      pitch toward level. Every other look device stops it (the mouse,
      the touch layer, the gyro); the Sense path did not. the user's log
      shows it plainly: hand=(p+52.0) sent=(p+24.8).
  (b) TWO aim frames. The sent angles used the RAW controller frame while
      the model, the laser and the muzzle used the frame after the global
      grip rotation (-20 deg). The barrel and the beam pointed 20 deg
      above the shot. There is now one named aim frame and everything
      derives from it; the per-weapon cosmetic pitch is gone for the same
      reason.

FIX 3 - barrel-true projectiles (charter A8, revised by the user).
QuakeQuest's engine-side origin shift around the QC think that fires,
with the wall handling it does not have: the shifted muzzle is traced
from the player's real muzzle and stopped short of solid, the shift is
magnitude-limited, and the origin is restored before SV_LinkEdict so
physics, collision and the network never see it. progs.dat untouched.

FIX 4 - the axe. The donor's table is in the Quake ENTITY frame where +Y
is LEFT; ours multiplies AngleVectors' right, which is -Y. Exactly one
weapon in the table has a lateral offset, so exactly one weapon was
wrong, mirrored and doubled: the axe, hanging off to the right of the
body. Also fixes the laser's "cone": the beam's half-width scaled with
the TOTAL trace length and sky is not solid to this trace, so aiming at
sky drew a 25-unit-wide red wedge from the muzzle to the horizon with
its impact dot 8192 units away.

FIX 5 - the viewmodel fallback can no longer consume an untracked pose;
with no hands it is placed from the HEAD, at the VR camera.

R3 - body-anchored holster zones (2 hip, 2 shoulder, 1 chest) as plain
geometry on R2's published hand state, in metres scaled by world scale.
Convenience: grip tap in a zone fires that zone's impulse. Immersive: the
aim grip IS the hand - press draws, release stows to the axe, press in
empty space re-draws. Either style: a long grip hold in a zone reassigns
it. Tracking loss or a menu releases everything and hands the weapon
back, so nobody is ever left axe-locked.

